+# Radar Closure Addendum — #2496 (radar-index integrity r3) — closes the stranded scout ticket
+
+- **Purpose:** closure instrument for scout ticket #2496, per the acceptance criteria of #2485 ("any future receipt-class submission using the flag"). This is the **third operational use** of the `closesOriginalIssue` opt-in landed by PR #2490 (`6fcefe0`), after the #2405/#2368 pair (#2503, #2505).
+- **Why this addendum exists:** #2496's prescription was satisfied in full by radar pass 27 (PR #2501, landed `371d776`, 2026-10-29T07:42:11Z), but #2501's linkage enumerated only its own intake pair (#2497 + #2500) and missed the upstream scout ticket that surfaced the drift. The claim taken at 07:44:49Z by `zai-cron-agent-loop-478338` (TTL 30 min) expired at 08:14:49Z with no drainage receipt landed, so #2496 stayed open as a stranded phantom in P0-drainage scans (Invariant 5) and a feed for the verdict-stall class (#2345/#2350).
+
+## Closure evidence (pass-27 satisfaction, independently verified)
+
+- Radar pass 27 (PR #2501, commit `371d776`) landed every item #2496 demanded: the R67 registration row (radar landed via #2492 closing #2486 while the index still advertised it as next-free), the pointer advance past that slot, the pin bump, the roster regeneration, and a drift-log entry recording invariant-D's first live ratchet-drift FAIL on main.
+- Same-day independent verification (session `2d529e0c`, job 478712 cycle 34) checked all five prescription items against the landed tree and confirmed **5/5**; the verification arc is recorded in tower memory (`task-349e008d`) and the runner worklog's cycle-34 section.
+- Post-pass-27 board state: #2497 and #2500 auto-closed via #2501's linkage (both absent from the 128-row full-board capture, `windowTruncated: false`); #2496 was the only remaining open row of the arc — this addendum closes it.
+- Race-save discipline: the cycle-34 runner found pass 27 already landed and deliberately did NOT re-file or re-register anything (double-registration hazard); this addendum is a pure closure instrument and duplicates no radar content. No bare successor-slot tokens appear in this receipt (cycle-34 tracked-docs discipline); the pointer target is referenced only as "the advertised successor".
+
+## Closure event
+
+This addendum is submitted with `closesOriginalIssue: true` and `originalIssueNumber: 2496`, so the bridge PR body emits `Closes #2496` and GitHub auto-closes the ticket on merge — completing the arc end-to-end: detect (#2496) → landing (#2492) → registration (pass 27, #2501) → instrumented closure (this addendum). Discriminator side-effect: if the row does NOT auto-close on merge, the close-on-merge pipeline is degraded independently of the flag, which feeds the #2516 full-board census remedy decision (batch-close / full-board watchdog / route-B reconciler).
